Scenario: View resynced closed watcher users on expired accounts
	Users on expired accounts who are resynced to Zendesk via Provisioning should be in their appropriate organization with their appropriate tags.

	Given I generate past static start and end dates
	And I update a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "DXP Production" to have the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticPastEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticPastOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticPastStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                     | |
	And I update a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "Gold Subscription" to have the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticPastEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticPastOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticPastStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                     | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Gold Subscription"
	And I assign the contact with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Closed Watcher |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Closed Watcher |
	Then the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be a watcher on an organization with the name "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be a watcher on an organization with the name "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not have the "osb_kb" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not have the "osb_kb" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not have the "osb_customer" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not have the "osb_customer" tag
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be in the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be in the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed to the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed to the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	Then I remove a user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" from an organization with the name "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I remove a user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" from an organization with the name "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I remove all tags from the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	And I remove all tags from the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	And I wait for "10" seconds
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "test@liferay.com" with password "nHZMPLWyzvRKujPLqfHK"
	And I go to the account index page
